<header><div class="wrap"><div class="brand">ROYCE<span>AI</span> SOLUTIONS</div>
<div class="nav"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/about/">About</a><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/roycekoh">LinkedIn</a></div></div></header>

<div class="wrap hero">
<h1>I deploy systems, then keep them working.<br><em>Anduril, Costa Mesa &amp; Irvine.</em></h1>
<p class="sub">Royce Koh — Irvine, CA. Fifteen years of professional experience in premium automotive operations, Seattle to Orange County, and since January 2026 the builder and operator of a production AI agent platform: conversational agents, RAG pipelines, multi-agent workflows and integrations to 20+ third-party services.</p>
<div class="pills"><span class="pill">Orange County local — relocated from Seattle</span><span class="pill">15 years experience</span><span class="pill">Agent &amp; automation systems</span><span class="pill">Field &amp; multi-site operations</span><span class="pill">Program management</span><span class="pill">English / Korean</span></div>
<div class="cta"><a class="btn p" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/roycekoh">LinkedIn</a><a class="btn s" href="mailto:royceaisolutions@gmail.com">Email me</a></div>
</div>

<section><div class="wrap">
<h2>Brands I have worked with</h2>
<p class="lead">Fifteen years representing premium, luxury and exotic brands.</p>
<div class="pills">
<span class="pill"><b>Ferrari</b></span>
<span class="pill"><b>Jaguar Land Rover</b></span>
<span class="pill"><b>Maserati</b></span>
<span class="pill"><b>BMW</b></span>
<span class="pill"><b>Toyota</b></span>
<span class="pill"><b>Lexus</b></span>
<span class="pill"><b>VinFast</b></span>
</div>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap">
<h2>Why Anduril, specifically</h2>
<p class="lead">Anduril's Orange County campus is where hardware, software and the field meet — and the jobs you are hiring for are the ones that decide whether a system works after it leaves the lab: <b>deployment, integration, automation, AI operations and program delivery</b>. I moved from Seattle to Orange County deliberately, and I have run operations in both markets — this is the one I chose to build in. That is where my career has been. At the dealerships I owned the outcome — the client, the schedule, the paperwork, the money — and for the last two years I have been on the other side of it, building the software: agents, pipelines, integrations and the monitoring that catches failures before a customer does.</p>
<p class="lead">I get systems into the real world, keep them running, and fix what breaks. And I already live ten minutes from Costa Mesa.</p>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap">
<h2>Inside the JLR systems — CRM, process, vehicle location</h2>
<p class="lead">At Jaguar Land Rover Newport Beach I do not just carry a client list. I am wired into the systems the store runs on, and everything a client hears from me comes out of them:</p>
<div class="sys">
<ul>
<li><b>CRM follow-up.</b> Every client relationship lives in <b>eLead CRM</b> — first contact, follow-up cadence, task queues, notes and outcomes. I work my own pipeline daily, so nothing goes cold and no follow-up is dropped.</li>
<li><b>Process and update management.</b> I own the record as the deal moves: order and allocation updates, delivery scheduling, status changes, and the internal handoffs between sales, F&amp;I, service and management. The system stays current because I keep it current.</li>
<li><b>Vehicle location.</b> I track units through <b>Dealergard / Stargard GPS</b> and inventory status — where the car actually is, in transit, on the lot, or at the shop — so a client gets an answer, not a guess.</li>
<li><b>Client communications.</b> All three feed the same thing: what I tell a client on a call, in a text, or in person is pulled from the live system record — accurate status, honest timing, no false expectations. That is how you keep a client after the sale.</li>
<li><b>Why it matters here.</b> The same discipline is what I bring to a deployment: understand the system of record, keep it true, and communicate from it — to the customer, the field team and the program office.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap">
<h2>What I bring</h2>
<div class="grid">
<div class="role"><div class="rt">Deployment &amp; field execution</div><p>Multi-site operations at VinFast (up to 15 locations, NorCal + SoCal), regional KPI ownership, logistics and delivery scheduling, and consignment inventory for ultra-high-net-worth clients where a single error is visible.</p></div>
<div class="role"><div class="rt">Production AI systems</div><p>RoyceAI platform: conversational agents, RAG pipelines, multi-agent workflows, persistent memory and skill architecture, integrations to 20+ third-party services — built and operated, not prototyped.</p></div>
<div class="role"><div class="rt">Automation that survives</div><p>180+ scheduled automations across ~200 environments with self-healing watchdogs, dedupe, and a rule I do not break: every change is verified against the live system before I call it done.</p></div>
<div class="role"><div class="rt">Operations metrics</div><p>AutoNation: 200% growth in vehicle acquisitions, 50% inventory improvement, 4,000 leads a month closing at 8–9%.</p></div>
<div class="role"><div class="rt">Communicating across the seam</div><p>I brief engineers and executives on the same system in the same hour — the skill that makes a deployment land instead of stall.</p></div>
<div class="role"><div class="rt">Operator mindset</div><p>Startup pace at VinFast, high-pressure retail, and my own company. I default to owning the problem, documenting it, and closing it out.</p></div>
</div>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap">
<h2>Where I fit — your live Orange County openings</h2>
<p class="lead">Every card below is a live Anduril posting in Irvine or Costa Mesa, linked straight to greenhouse and verified open today. I screened each one before linking it: no active-clearance requirement I cannot meet, no engineering-domain requirement I would be pretending to have, and a posted band that clears $15K a month at the top of range. The line under each role is what they ask for and what I have done.</p>
<div class="grid">
<a class="role" href="https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/5195990007?gh_jid=5195990007" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><div class="rt">Manager, Business Operations, Air Defense</div><div class="rl">Irvine, California &middot; $146K–$194K</div><p>They want 5+ years running operations for a business line. I ran up to 15 VinFast locations and 100 salespeople with P&amp;L ownership, then delivered 200% acquisition growth and 50% inventory improvement at AutoNation.</p></a>
<a class="role" href="https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/4951325007?gh_jid=4951325007" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><div class="rt">Business Operations Lead</div><div class="rl">Costa Mesa, California &middot; $146K–$150K</div><p>The ask is six years of cross-functional operations ownership; I have fifteen. I built the CRM, inventory and delivery workflows — and I still run the automation layer that keeps them reporting.</p></a>
<a class="role" href="https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/5204204007?gh_jid=5204204007" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><div class="rt">Logistics Program Manager</div><div class="rl">Costa Mesa, California &middot; $146K–$194K</div><p>Program-managing logistics across a system's life is what I did at scale: inventory, delivery scheduling and high-value consignment across up to 15 locations, with cost and schedule visible every week.</p></a>
<a class="role" href="https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/5005173007?gh_jid=5005173007" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><div class="rt">Deployment Operations Manager</div><div class="rl">Costa Mesa, California &middot; $129K–$171K</div><p>I have deployed operations repeatedly — new stores, new systems, EV charging infrastructure — and documented each one so the next launch was faster and repeatable.</p></a>
<a class="role" href="https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/5079152007?gh_jid=5079152007" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><div class="rt">IT Operations Manager, M&amp;A</div><div class="rl">Costa Mesa, California &middot; $129K–$171K</div><p>The systems side of integration is my daily work: 20+ third-party services wired together, 100+ automations in production with self-healing monitoring. Post-acquisition integration is the same problem at company scale.</p></a>
<a class="role" href="https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/5117374007?gh_jid=5117374007" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><div class="rt">Business Operations Lead - Technical Projects</div><div class="rl">Costa Mesa, California &middot; band not posted</div><p>Technical project operations: I translate between engineers and the business, keep deliverables moving, and I am Google Project Management certified.</p></a>
</div>
</div></section>

