<section><div class="wrap">
<h2>How I work</h2>
<ul class="clean">
<li><b>Ship, then verify.</b> I read the live system back before I call a change done.</li>
<li><b>Write it down.</b> Every system I run carries its own reasoning in plain text, so the next person can pick it up.</li>
<li><b>Handle the unglamorous work.</b> Logs, edge cases, the customer who is angry at 7pm — that is the job.</li>
<li><b>Ask before assuming.</b> If I do not know the requirement, I get it in writing and confirm it back.</li>
</ul>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap">
<h2>Straight talk</h2>
<div class="talk">
<p style="margin:0 0 10px"><b>Certified.</b> Google IT Support and Google Project Management. The credential I lean on is the platform running in production right now.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 10px"><b>Local.</b> Fifteen years in the business, including the Seattle market. Relocated to Orange County and settled in Irvine — ten minutes from the Costa Mesa campus, fifteen from the Irvine sites. I can be on site in person, quickly.</p>
<p style="margin:0"><b>Eligibility.</b> Several Anduril roles require U.S. person status or clearance eligibility. Tell me the requirement and I will confirm my status honestly and immediately — I would rather answer that question in the first email than in the fifth interview.</p>
</div>
</div></section>

